{"id":"f07a40d40db38dd68d349d9cc580019ef88c16c06d2dc34716e695b1e7f433e2","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-10T12:12:27.968901788Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## What to build\n\nTwo pieces. (a) A contract test inside the CLI crate that feeds every command documented in the agent guide, the help text and the hint lines emitted in `--markdown` output through the real clap parser, so a rename or wrong flag fails at build time. (b) One shared module that owns \"resolve the ticket, run a mutation, render as JSON, Markdown or a human line\", plus one argument group for ticket selection and output format, replacing the tail repeated in about 15 mutation commands.\n\n## Why\n\nThe `ti close -t <id>` problem happened because the agent guide documented a form the CLI rejected and nothing tied docs to clap. `close` was patched to accept both forms, but the contract is still untested. Ticket selection has three shapes across commands (flag only, positional only, both) and the same JSON/Markdown tail is repeated in many commands. The Checked-out ticket rule has no single owner: `close` clears it but `ti state closed:…` and the TUI close do not, although CONTEXT.md says it may be a Closed ticket.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test parses every `ti …` command in the agent guide, the help template and the render hint strings; it fails if one is rejected (demonstrate by breaking one temporarily)\n- [ ] Mutation commands use one shared tail and one argument group; the per-command copies are deleted\n- [ ] The shared tail has a single test instead of one per command\n- [ ] Decision recorded in the PR: whether closing clears the Checked-out ticket consistently (CLI, `state`, TUI)\n- [ ] `--json`/`--markdown` output contract (stdout only, no ANSI, non-zero on failure) unchanged; existing CLI tests pass\n\n## Blocked by\n\nNone — can start immediately. The contract-test half can land first on its own.\n\n## Notes\n\nModest depth gain; the contract test is worthwhile regardless. Related existing ticket: \"CLI-wide sentinel for the checked-out ticket\" (2ee5e0). The crate is binary-only, so the test must live inside the crate."}}}